  "prefLabel": "Rko 214.06 Requests for Rehearing or Reconsideration",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rko 214.06 Requests for Rehearing or Reconsideration.\n\n(a) No later than 30 days from the date appearing on a decision, a party may file with the ombudsman a request for rehearing or reconsideration.\n\n(b) Requests for rehearing or reconsideration shall:\n\n(1) Be in the form of a written motion addressed to the ombudsman;\n\n(2) Be delivered to the presiding officer, all persons who have filed an appearance in the case and any person who has filed an amicus brief;\n\n(3) Specify all grounds upon which it is claimed that the original decision is unlawful or unreasonable; and\n\n(4) Identify the issues to be addressed upon rehearing or reconsideration.\n\nSource. #13921, eff 5-20-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rko100-200.html"
